## Architecture notes

- Tenant isolation is enforced at the database layer via RLS
- All secrets are sourced from Doppler — nothing is committed
- The Control Plane client in `packages/api-client` communicates with KORAS
  Control Plane for provisioning and entitlement checks
- ZITADEL JWT is validated on every API request in `services/api`

{{#if capability.ai}}## The assistant

This product was generated with the `ai` capability. The runtime is the
`koras_ai` package; this product's own agents, tools, prompts, knowledge sources
and model catalogue live in `services/api/koras_api/ai/` and nowhere else.
Product code names model aliases and never a provider's model; nothing in this
repository calls a provider directly, holds a provider key or decides an
authorization from a model's output. A tool declares the permission it needs
and its operation class, and anything that is not a read waits for a person.
The starter's `docs/AI_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` is the guide.

