### Two sets of agents, and which one is current

The canonical agent architecture is the **40 definitions under
`.claude/agents/<category>/`** — 7 planning, 9 development, 10 testing,
5 review, 2 documentation, 6 delivery, 1 orchestration. They are registered in
`.claude/orchestration/agent-registry.yaml`, which is the authority on the
count, and the orchestration contract routes to them by capability. Almost all
of them stay dormant for any given feature; invoking all 40 is a defect in
orchestration, not diligence.

The **four files at the top of `.claude/agents/`** — `architect.md`,
`frontend.md`, `reviewer.md`, `tester.md` — predate that architecture. They
carry no agent frontmatter, so Claude Code does not register them as agents,
and they are deliberately not part of the 40. They are retained because
`/feature`, `/review`, `/test` and `/ui-review` still read them, and deleting
them would break four working commands to tidy a directory listing. Treat them
as guidance for those commands and as nothing else: they are not the catalogue,
they are not a shorter version of it, and a count of this repository's agents
is 40, not 44.

### Before implementing anything

1. Read `.koras/project.yaml`. It is the authoritative record of which profile
   this repository is — `{{profile}}` — and takes precedence over the directory
   name, the git remote, or an inference from the code.
2. Load `.claude/CLAUDE.md` for the shared rules.
3. Load `koras-profile-product` for the rules specific to this profile. Where it is
   narrower than the shared rules, it wins.
4. Read `docs/AGENT_CONTEXT.md` if it exists. It holds rules this
   repository wrote for itself, and it outranks the shared ones.
5. Search this repository before creating anything. Reuse the existing
   component, hook, client, schema, service or pattern.

### Project-specific rules

Everything in `.claude/` and this file is generator-owned and will be
overwritten by `create-koras-app --refresh`. Rules this repository writes for
itself belong in `docs/AGENT_CONTEXT.md`, which the generator never writes and
never overwrites.

Read it if it exists. Where it contradicts the shared rules, it wins -- it is
the narrower, more local statement of how this specific repository works.

